<p>
Each deposit file lists one or more mineral/rock entries, each with a host-rock reference
(<code>attributes.inblock</code>, sometimes a wildcard covering many rock types via
<code>allowedVariants</code>) and a placed-block template (<code>attributes.placeblock</code>)
that may itself vary by grade (poor/medium/rich/bountiful). Every host-rock × grade combination is
expanded into its own concrete block code so a page like "chromite in andesite" is distinct from
"chromite in kimberlite", since real grade ranges genuinely differ per rock.
</p>
<p>
This is a worldgen-only catalog: it covers every rock/grade combination the deposit files declare,
regardless of whether that exact block is otherwise reachable from a recipe or drop table (most
aren't, directly -- you mine the ore block first).
</p>
